WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.401 line:92%
-Hello, Elizabeth. How are you

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:04.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am so happy to be here.
How you guys doing?

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:07.173 size:84% position:42%
-Well, I'm very excited
to talk about the show,

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I also am very excited
about this.

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are joining us
right after your first

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:14.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
dentist appointment
in -- in months.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:15.715 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's right.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.717 size:81% position:41%
-And we are just dying
to know how it went.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:20.320 line:92%
-I have a temporary crown.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:24.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had three cracks
in a back tooth

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:28.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
that have sort of been achin
for like six months.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:28.962 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughs ]

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:32.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I finally thought,
"I better go get it handled.

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.801 line:92%
I can actually smile, mostly

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:38.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you can see
it's a little off still.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:41.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I had a really hard time
putting my lipstick on,

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:42.909 line:92%
but I think I did all right.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:43.710 line:92%
I don't know. I can't tell

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:48.181
-I bet if we hadn't brought it
up, no one would've noticed.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
So thank you for that then

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:52.118 line:92%
-I meant every word of it.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.354 size:88% position:44%
This is -- I want to ask
about "Press Your Luck."

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a game show
from the '80s.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.526
And, first of all, it looks like
a lot of fun to host.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:03.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
Second, is it weird
looking at old episodes

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you are not just
with an audience of people

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:10.470
but an audience of people
having a very good time

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.173 line:92%
and projecting their joy?

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:13.973 line:92%
-Yeah. I -- I actually --

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:17.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
I read a tweet, recently,
from a "Press Your Luck" fan

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:19.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
that said,
"Elizabeth is always yelling."

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:21.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you
for that judgment, one.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:25.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
Two, it's because the audience
loves this show.

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:29.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
They are raucous.
I mean, you know, they're --

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:32.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're so happy when someon
wins a car, as am I.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:36.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're so happy to se
the Whammy, as am I.

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:38.164 line:92%
And so it's really, really loud.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:41.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the idea
of making the show --

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:42.535 size:88% position:44% line:92%
In the future, I mean --

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:44.938 size:81% position:41%
I know that we can get
contestants in there,

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:47.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, you know,
I will definitely miss

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:51.711
the live, in-studio audience
as I imagine you do, as well

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:53.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
getting through your jokes
every night.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:56.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do.
I feel like a lot of my joke

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.884 size:84% position:42% line:92%
are getting Whammies --

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
based on not having
an audience here.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:01.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was this a show
you watched growing up?

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:04.724
Because I have a lot of memories
of "Press Your Luck."

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:07.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh. It was the
after-school, like, specia

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:11.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
that me and my sibs
needed to watch every day.

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:12.031 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We -- I loved --

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:15.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
When they first presented it
to me, I was like, "Wait.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:16.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're going to
bring back this show

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was my favorite thing
in the world?"

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.607 line:92%
And then, also, the Whammies

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:23.610 size:88% position:44%
We -- We kept a lot of
the old animation style.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:27.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's got this
really kitschy Whammy to i

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
that just brings back
so many memories.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.985
It was one of those things where
we just piled onto the couch

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:35.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
We ate Lucky Charms,
which we were not allowed.

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was, like,
our Saturday morning cereal,

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:38.925 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but we'd sneak it.

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:41.194 size:84% position:42%
And we would pick out
all of the marshmallows

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:43.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
out of the Lucky Charms
and watch "Press Your Luck."

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:47.233
That is like -- Those are, like,
gold memories in my brain.

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:49.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It seems like it must be a jo
to do this job now,

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:52.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, of course, you did no
set out to be a game-show host

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:54.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's sort of a nice byproduc
of being an actor.

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:57.310
Was that something you alway
thought you were going to do

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.811 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is pursue acting?

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, no, I didn't decide
to be an actor --

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
Really, I didn't decide
to be an actor

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:03.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
until I was halfway
through college.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:08.621
And I thought I would be
Diane Sawyer or Barbara Walters.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:11.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wanted to be --
I wanted to basic--

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:13.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or be you.
I wanted to do that job.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:18.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I got to play
to great effect on "30 Rock,

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:20.400 line:92%
and in many other roles now --

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.968 line:92%
I have played a newscaster

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:25.104 size:78% position:39%
I thought I would do,
like, broadcast news.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:28.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are very good
as a comedy newscaster.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
I -- Maybe that means
that you wouldn't

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
have been perfect
for the real thing,

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:32.612 line:92%
but you are as good at comedy --

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:36.683 size:88% position:44%
You are the Diane Sawyer
of comedy newscasters.

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:37.483 line:92%
-Thank you. Yeah, they --

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was very happy
when Tina Fey sent me

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:43.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
to North Korea
to do the news there.

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:44.157 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-And you actually went.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:45.692 size:84% position:42%
A lot of people thought
that was green screen,

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:47.393 size:84% position:42%
but you did actually --
-People don't realize.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was in -- Yeah.
I actually went there.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.931 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-You -- You've also have

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
made quite a career
as a producer.

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.802
You have a production compan
called "Brownstone" that -

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:59.339
among other things,
the "Pitch Perfect" franchise --

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:01.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
has tried really hard
to give voice

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:02.976 line:92%
to, you know, especially women

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:07.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
and people who have less
of a voice in this industry,

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.147 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
you know, still do.

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:10.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I was wondering
how much you've seen it change

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:12.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the last ten years
that you've been doing it?

00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:14.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I actually think
in the last --

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:18.057
I've been doing it, yeah,
a little more than a decade now.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:19.425 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And I think, actually,

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
we've made a lot
of incredible progress.

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:25.164
I think that the amount
of television and content

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:27.867 size:75% position:38%
that's being created
is really incredible

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:29.869 line:92%
in this moment in time anyway.

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:32.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
But making
especially feature films

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:36.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
that feature large casts
of women

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:38.044 line:92%
is still very, very rare.

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:39.178 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And so to have made

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:43.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Pitch Perfect"
and "Charlie's Angels" --

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:45.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, if that's my legac
of creating things

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:50.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
and telling women's stories,
female-fronted stories --

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:53.026 size:81% position:41%
We also have "Shrill,"
starring Aidy Bryant.

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:56.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just think
I will be very happy

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:58.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
if that's my legacy
in Hollywood.

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:01.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a pretty good legacy
and it's really well-deserved.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:03.002 line:92%
Before you go, I want to ask

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:06.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we both
are parents of two boys.

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:07.840 line:92%
Yours are a little older.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:08.574 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How is --

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:12.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
How is school going
as we now are in the fall?

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:17.950
-Well, I am still having trouble
getting them to wear pants

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.185 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yep.

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:20.386 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-And -- [ Laughs ]

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:24.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my son wore
a ninja costume

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:26.826 size:78% position:39% line:92%
last week for school.

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:30.630
Just -- I just walked in,
and he was in a full ninja

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:31.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the best part
about it, Seth,

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:34.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
was I sat there
for a minute to be like,

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:36.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Is this okay that
he's in a ninja costume?"

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:37.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then
they went around the room,

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:40.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
and another kid
was wearing a ninja costume.

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:44.510
Like, full, like, Cobra Ka
with the red and everything.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:47.447 line:92%
And my son was like, "What?!

00:05:47.447 --> 00:05:50.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, looked at me, like,
"That's MY thing!"

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:54.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it turns out
he wasn't the only one.

00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:55.088 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughs ]

00:05:55.088 --> 00:05:56.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
-As they get older,
they'll realize ninjas

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:59.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
shouldn't really present
themselves on Zoom like that

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:02.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know? You have to be
a little bit more secretive.

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:04.163 line:92%
-Little more secretive. Yeah

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:05.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was in the full black
ninja costume.

00:06:05.832 --> 00:06:09.001
The fact that this other kid
was also wearing a ninja costume

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:10.169 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
just broke me.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:11.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
I walked in the other day,

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:14.173 size:78% position:39%
and my son was, like,
sitting on his side,

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:15.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, on his elbow
wearing a straw hat.

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:18.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he looked like
a Carly Simon record album

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:22.415
So we're all -- Everybody'
getting good looks at their kids

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:25.685 size:84% position:42%
that we wouldn't get on
a normal school day.

00:06:25.685 --> 00:06:29.555
-We're really delving into
some, like, psyche, you know

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:33.626
It's -- It's like what the
wished school was actually like.

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:35.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know?
-Absolutely. Hey.

00:06:35.495 --> 00:06:37.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
All the best to your family.
Congrats on the show.

00:06:37.597 --> 00:06:39.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always lovely
to talk to you, Elizabeth.

00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:43.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you. "Press Your Luck
on Thursday, everybody!

